          translation: `However, to enter a higher school was still what I longed for. Thus I secretly gained admission to a normal school and would only dare to tell my mother the truth on condition that the school offered a uniform, board, books, and accommodation. Yet I had to pay a cash deposit of ten yuan for enrollment, which was an enormous figure for us then. Nevertheless, mother managed to get the money after half a month’s borrowing around and sent me off with tears. She spared no pains to bring me a bright future. The night when I graduated from the normal school and was assigned principal of an elementary school, both mother and I were sleepless. The only thing I said to my mother was “From now on, you can lead a life of leisure!” Her answer was no other than trickles of tears.`,
